 "schema": "tiles3/ground-types@1",
 "_comment": "The Ground-type model, per the maintainer (2026-08-21): a Ground type has base tiles (one, several, or a single colour), 'on top of' (the x-over-y matrix in tiles/review), and transitions (tiles/transitions). base_color is what a field reads as; base_tiles is the maintainer's promoted list - EMPTY until he promotes (candidates wait in tiles/base_candidates/<ground>/, colour-corrected exactly as the game draws them). always_own_texture mirrors transition_surface=='base': such a ground looks deliberately repeated (paving, parquet) and its transition tiles mimic the neighbouring field. surface=='flat' grounds have no base tile yet and draw the single colour - 'the trick we use when we have still not found that perfect texture' - probably permanent for lava/water/deep_water, which the game animates. A field repeats ONE base tile; variation only ever comes from base tiles that look the same.",
